/-!
# The 3D gauge-fixed gravity Hamiltonian in the jet coordinates, **through Faris–Lavine**

`BookProof.ChapterQg3DGaugeEsa` proves essential self-adjointness of the `84`-coordinate
3D gauge-fixed gravity Hamiltonian — the densitized, Weyl-ordered Hamiltonian whose
coordinates are the four spacetime coordinates, the sixteen tetrad components `e_μ^a` and
the sixty-four **independent coordinates `E_{μν}^a` representing the spatial derivatives of
the tetrad** — by the Carleman flux criterion.  That criterion does not lift to the outer
Fock space.  This module re-proves the same statement, and strengthens it, using **only**
the commutator criterion of Faris–Lavine with the Friedrichs extension of
`N₁ = −Δ + ‖x‖²/4` as comparison operator, which does lift.

## What is proved

* `qgSigned_eq_sqSumOp` — the identification: for every real signature `κ` the operator
  `½ Σ_j κ_j π_j² + ½ Σ_m T_m²` is the kinetic-plus-squares operator `sqSumOp κ torsionVec`.
* **`qgSigned_esa_fl`**, **`qg3D_esa_fl`** — essential self-adjointness on the
  Gauss–polynomial core of `L²(ℝ⁸⁴)`, by Faris–Lavine, for every real signature and in
  particular for the physical hyperbolic signature `qgKappa`.
* `div3Vec`, `timeDerivVec`, `qgGaugeVec` — the two gauge-fixing families, written as linear
  forms in the `84` coordinates: the **3D gauge condition** `Σ_j E_{jj}^a = 0` (the spatial
  divergence of the tetrad, expressed in the coordinates that represent its spatial
  derivatives) and the **gauge fixing of the derivative coordinates** `E_{0ν}^a = 0` (the
  coordinates representing time derivatives are fixed to zero, which is what makes the
  formulation three-dimensional).
* **`qg3DGaugeFixed_esa_fl`** — the gauge-fixed Hamiltonian, torsion *and* both gauge-fixing
  families together, is essentially self-adjoint on the core, by Faris–Lavine.
* **`qgGaugeOuterHam`, `qgGauge_sector_esa_fl`, `qgGauge_outerHam_esa_fl`** — the same
  Hamiltonian on the nested Fock space `⊕ₙ L²(ℝ^{84n})`, one copy of the one-particle
  Hamiltonian per particle, essentially self-adjoint on the finite-particle core.
* **`qg3DGaugeFixed_stone_flow`, `qgGauge_stone_flow`** — the unitary time evolution
  generated by the unique self-adjoint realization, on the one-particle space and on the
  nested Fock space (Stone).
* **`dsOp_number_conserving`, `qgGauge_number_conserving`** — the outer Hamiltonian
  **conserves the particle number**: it is block diagonal in the particle-number sectors, and
  its restriction to the `n`-particle sector is the `n`-particle Hamiltonian
  (`qgGaugeOuterHam_sector`).  This is what makes a spatial lattice regularization
  unnecessary: the sectors, not a lattice, cut the problem into pieces.

## Scope — this model carries **no scalaron**

The identification `qgSigned_eq_sqSumOp` of the Hamiltonian as a *kinetic-plus-squares*
operator is a statement about the pure tetrad/jet sector: kinetic term plus squares of
**linear** forms in the `84` coordinates.  It does **not** extend to the gravity Hamiltonian
this development delivers, which also carries the scalaron with the **full exponential**
Einstein-frame potential and no Taylor expansion: that potential is not a polynomial of
degree `≤ 2`, hence not a half-sum of squares of linear forms
(`BookProof.ScalaronNotQuadratic.starobinskyV_not_quadratic`,
`starobinskyPot_not_sum_of_squares`), so no kinetic-plus-squares identification of it is
possible or claimed.  The Hamiltonian with the vielbein, the scalaron, the 3D gauge fixing
and the gauge fixing of the derivative variables is
`BookProof.QgVielbeinScalaronGaugeFL.secHam _ (qgFullModes g)`, whose essential
self-adjointness on the outer Fock space is proved by Faris–Lavine against a comparison
operator whose fibre carries the exponential wall itself.

No spectral information and no mass gap is claimed.

Everything is `sorry`-free and `axiom`-free.
-/

